# Paranal Airglow Line And Continuum Emission (PALACE) model: data and code of
# v1.0 (Noll et al. 2024)
# 
# PALACE reference intensities for atomic lines (consistent with corresponding
# lines in palace_lines.fits)
# 
# Column names:
# lam: vacuum wavelength in µm (NIST)
# trans: atmospheric transmission for standard conditions at Cerro Paranal
#        (noll+12), PWV = 2.5 mm, and zenith
# fH2O: fraction of H2O with respect to optical depth (based on transmission
#       spectra with PWV = 1 and 5 mm)
# I: reference intensity in R
# ID: 12 characters describing upper and lower states (NIST):
#     1-2: chemical species
#     3-4: last subshell of configuration of upper state
#     5-6: term of upper state
#     7-8: last subshell of configuration of lower state
#     9-10: term of lower state
#     11: quantum number J of upper state multiplied by 2 (O: 1)
#     12: quantum number J of lower state multiplied by 2 (O: 1)
# chem: chemical species (Na, K, O, N, or H)
# M: molar mass in kg/mol
# Tkin: kinetic temperature in K for Doppler broadening of line
# hlay: height of emission layer in km (H: -1)
# src: 4-digit binary code for source of intensity I:
#      1: I based on X-shooter data (partly noll+23)? 1 = yes, 0 = no
#      2: I based on UVES data from noll+20? 1 = yes, 0 = no
#      3: I based on other data (cosby+06, oliva+15)? 1 = yes, 0 = no
#      4: I based on model (= 1) or direct measurement (= 0)?
# class: label of variability class
# 
# References:
# NIST: https://physics.nist.gov/asd
# noll+12: https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/201219040
# noll+19: https://doi.org/10.1029/2018JD030044 (only K lines)
# 
